<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan sugar output reaches 1.17 million tonnes.</title>
<headline>Pakistan sugar output reaches 1.17 million tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Pakistan Sugar Mills Association said on Sunday sugar production had reached 1.17 million tonnes by January 31, 22 percent down on the 1.5 million tonnes produced by the same date last year.</p>
<p>One dealer said output had fallen because sugar mills had delayed the start of the crushing season to November, instead of October, in hopes of increasing the yield from sugarcane.</p>
<p>The association said mills hoped to produce 2.65 million tonnes in 1996/97 (July-June), compared to 2.47 million in 1995/96 and 3.0 million in 1994/95.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
